*The driver's `META-INF/services/java.sql.Driver` entry lets `DriverManager` find it automatically.*

```java
// every call pays the full TCP + authentication cost
for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
    try (Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection(url, user, pass)) {
        // ... do one small query, then the connection is destroyed
    }
}
```

```java
// HikariCP keeps connections open; getConnection() borrows one
for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
    try (Connection con = dataSource.getConnection()) {
        // ... do one small query; close() returns it to the pool, not destroyed
    }
}
```

*Same loop, but the pooled DataSource avoids 1,000 expensive handshakes.*

```java
String sql = "SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE city = ?";
try (Connection con = dataSource.getConnection();              // 1
     PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql)) {        // 2
    ps.setString(1, "Pune");                                    // 3 bind
    try (ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) {                    // 3 execute (SELECT)
        while (rs.next()) {                                     // 4
            System.out.println(rs.getInt("id") + ": " + rs.getString("name"));
        }
    }
}                                                              // 5 auto-close

// for INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE use executeUpdate (returns row count):
// int rows = ps.executeUpdate();
```

```java
DataSource ds = ...;                                  // DataSource
try (Connection con = ds.getConnection();             // Connection
     PreparedStatement ps =                             // PreparedStatement
         con.prepareStatement("SELECT name FROM users WHERE id = ?")) {
    ps.setLong(1, 7L);
    try (ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) {           // ResultSet
        if (rs.next()) System.out.println(rs.getString("name"));
    }
}
// Every type above is an interface; the JDBC driver supplies the classes.
```

